{{Quote|General, are you seeing this?|Connix, to Leia Organa during the Battle of Starkiller Base|<ref name="Episode VII" />}}
'''Kaydel Ko Connix''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] who lived during the era of the [[New Republic Era|New Republic]] and the subsequent [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]]. [[Reproduction|Born]] on [[Dulathia]], Connix ultimately joined the Resistance; and was stationed at their [[D'Qar]] [[Resistance base|headquarters]]. Serving under [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], a veteran of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] and leader of the Resistance, she worked as an operations [[controller]] in [[Fleet Command (Resistance)|Fleet Command]].

Connix's service resulted in her promotion to [[lieutenant]] following the [[Battle of Starkiller Base]]. Anticipating a First Order retaliatory strike, Connix was entrusted with supervising the [[Battle of D'Qar|evacuation]] of D'Qar. After narrowly escaping the [[planet]] just prior to the base's destruction, she resumed her responsibilities as a [[sensor]] ops [[officer]] aboard the [[MC85 Star Cruiser|Star Cruiser]] [[Raddus (MC85 Star Cruiser)|''Raddus'']].

During the [[Battle of Oetchi|flight]] of the [[Resistance navy|Resistance fleet]], Connix was one of several [[Resistance officer|officers]] who supported [[Poe Dameron]]'s [[Treason|mutiny]] against Admiral [[Amilyn Holdo|Holdo]]. Their efforts ultimately failed, however, when Dameron was [[Stun|incapacitated]] by Organa herself. Despite their mutiny, Connix and Dameron remained in service to the Resistance during the [[Battle of Crait]]. They were among the few survivors who escaped the battle aboard the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''.

Connix remained a lieutenant in the Resistance, putting her past as a mutineer behind her and regaining the trust of Organa. She helped set up the [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|Resistance base]] on [[Ajan Kloss]], and later participated in the [[battle of Exegol]]. After surviving the battle, she celebrated with the rest of the Resistance.

==Biography==
===Outbreak of war===
{{Quote|Punch it!|Connix, during the evacuation of D'Qar|<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>}}
[[File:TFA_Resdox_behind_Connix.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Connix earned a promotion to lieutenant as a result of her service during the Starkiller crisis.]]
[[Reproduction|Born]] around [[13 ABY]],<ref name="Birth year" /> Kaydel Ko Connix was a [[Homeworld|native]] of [[Dulathia]].<ref name="TLJVD" /> As [[Politics|political]] relations [[Cold War|worsened]] between the [[New Republic]] and the [[First Order]], the latter was opposed by [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], who founded a private military group known as the [[Resistance]] to monitor the First Order's activities.<ref name="Resistance">{{Databank|the-resistance|The Resistance}}</ref> Connix ultimately joined the [[Resistance navy|naval branch]] of the Resistance and was assigned to [[Fleet Command (Resistance)|Fleet Command]].<ref name="TLJVD" /> By [[34 ABY]],<ref name="GA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> Connix was serving as an operations [[controller]] under the direct command of Organa,<ref name="TLJVD" /> who&mdash;in her capacity as leader of the Resistance&mdash;assumed the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[general]].<ref name="Episode VII" />

Following the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]] and the [[Battle of Takodana]], the Resistance [[Battle of Starkiller Base|attacked]] [[Starkiller Base]] in the hope of destroying the [[superweapon]].<ref name="Episode VII" /> During the battle, Connix coordinated communications<ref name="Connix" /> between the resistance [[pilot]]s and their [[commander]]s from the [[Resistance base]] on [[D'Qar]].<ref name="Episode VII" /> After the destruction of Starkiller Base, Connix was promoted to the rank of [[lieutenant]] in recognition of her service as an operations controller; and was tasked with overseeing the [[Battle of D'Qar|D'Qar evacuation]]; prioritizing the recovery of supplies, and coordinating an organized retreat.<ref name="TLJVD" /> She was still on the planet's surface when the [[First Order Navy]] invaded the [[Ileenium system|system]]. The base was destroyed from [[orbit]] by the [[Mandator IV-class Siege Dreadnought|Dreadnought]] ''[[Fulminatrix]]'', although Connix managed to escape just in [[time]] on one of the last departing [[U-55 orbital loadlifter|shuttles]]. After boarding the [[MC85 Star Cruiser]] [[Raddus (MC85 Star Cruiser)|''Raddus'']], she returned to her duties as an operations controller.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

[[File:LieutenantKaydelConnix.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Following the destruction of Starkiller Base, Connix oversaw the preparations to evacuate D'Qar.]]
While the Resistance [[fleet]] [[Battle of Oetchi|fled]] from the First Order, including the First Order's [[flagship]] ''[[Supremacy]]'', [[Poe Dameron]] enlisted Connix's assistance for an unauthorized [[Mission to Canto Bight|mission]]&mdash;to help [[Finn]] and [[Rose Tico]] disable the First Order's [[hyperspace]] [[Hyperspace tracker|tracking system]]. Using her position on the [[Starship|ship's]] [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]], Connix ensured that their departure went unnoticed by [[Vice Admiral]] [[Amilyn Holdo|Holdo]]. After discovering Holdo's intention to evacuate the crew of the ''Raddus'', Connix and several [[Resistance officer]]s supported Dameron's [[Treason|mutiny]] against Holdo. With the [[admiral]] and her supporters detained at [[blaster]] point, Connix and Dameron seized control of the bridge. However, they were ultimately confronted by a recovered Organa. Using the [[stun]] setting on her [[Blaster pistol|blaster]], the general shot Dameron and accepted Connix's surrender.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

Despite her role in the conspiracy against Holdo, Connix continued to serve the Resistance and was among the survivors who took control of an abandoned [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] [[Crait outpost|outpost]] on [[Crait]]. The ensuing [[Battle of Crait|battle]] marked the near destruction of the Resistance. However, Connix was able to escape with Organa, Dameron, and several other survivors aboard the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

===Further service===
{{Quote|We'd be no more than bugs to them.|Connix, prior to the Battle of Exegol|<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>}}
[[File: AjanKloss-TROS.png|thumb|left|300px|Connix assisted in the construction of the Resistance Base located on Ajan Kloss.]]
After the battle on Crait, Connix put the mutiny behind her. She was still trusted by Organa and retained her rank<ref name="SWCT 2020 base">{{SWCT|set=2020 Base Series|cardname=Kaydel Ko Connix}}</ref> though the general was disappointed that Connix had supported Dameron's actions. However, Organa knew she had meant well, and forgave her.<ref name="Resistance Reborn">''[[Resistance Reborn]]''</ref> During her time at the [[Resistance Camp]] on the garbage planet of [[Anoat]], Connix witnessed the [[destruction of Tah'Nuhna]] and informed General Organa. She also assured Organa that the General had done everything she could and it wasn't her fault, pointing at their main mission of protecting as many as they can as long as they were still alive.<ref name="Allegiance 1">[[Allegiance 1|''Allegiance'' 1]]</ref> Later, she also informed General [[Jonato]] about a [[First Order]] armada heading towards [[Mon Cala]] where General Organa, [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], Rose Tico, and [[C-3PO]] had gone on a mission. Jonato wanted to contact and warn Organa but Connix informed him that the First Order was also blocking communication across the system.<ref name="Allegiance 3">[[Allegiance 3|''Allegiance'' 3]]</ref>

[[File:RoseBeaumontKaydel-CGSWG.png|thumb|right|220px|Connix during the Battle of Exegol.]]
Sometime later, Connix helped Tico and [[Beaumont Kin]] establish a new [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|base]] on [[Ajan Kloss]].<ref name="TROSVD" /> In [[35 ABY]], when the Resistance heard word of [[Darth Sidious]]' return on the [[Sith]] world [[Exegol]], they sent a force to [[Battle of Exegol|destroy]] him before he could escape the planet. Connix, alongside Tico and Kin, participated in the assault on the [[Sith Eternal]]'s navigation tower on the ''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer [[Steadfast (Resurgent-class)|''Steadfast'']]. During the assault, Connix injured her leg and was helped back to the [[Fortitude (transport)|''Fortitude'']] by Kin. She later celebrated the end of the First Order at the Resistance base alongside Tico and Kin.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|She's running away!''"<br />"''No she isn't.|Connix and Poe Dameron, witnessing Amilyn Holdo's sacrifice|<ref name="Episode VIII" />}}
[[File:BillieLourd1.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Connix sporting blonde buns and a junior controller's uniform circa 34 ABY.]]
Kaydel Ko Connix was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]]<ref name="Connix" /> with light skin, [[Color|brown]] [[eye]]s, and blonde [[hair]] which she wore up in two buns.<ref name="Episode VII" /> By the time of [[35 ABY]], Connix's hair had turned brown.<ref name="Episode IX" /> Like many other female [[Resistance]] women, she was influenced by [[Resistance]] leader [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia's]] hairstyle and wore her hair wrapped around her head like a crown.<ref name="Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> Her service as an operations controller was viewed favorably by her superiors, resulting in Connix's rise to the rank of lieutenant.<ref name="TLJVD" /> However, while serving under Amilyn Holdo, Connix sympathized with Poe Dameron's misgivings about the Vice Admiral's leadership style. Her support for Dameron led Connix to engage in activities ranging from conspiracy<ref name="Connix" /> to open rebellion against Holdo. After abandoning the ''Raddus'' during the First Order's assault on the Resistance fleet, Connix watched as Holdo altered course and assumed that the Vice Admiral was trying to save herself. In reality, Holdo was intending to ram the ''Supremacy''.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

==Equipment==
As an officer of the Resistance, Connix wore a brown [[Clothing|junior controller's uniform]], a [[comlink]] [[headset]],<ref name="TFAVD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> and was armed with a blaster [[pistol]].<ref name="Connix" /> After her promotion, Connix's received a brown officer's uniform that included her lieutenant [[Resistance rank badge|rank badge]].<ref name="TLJVD" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Kaydel_Ko_Connix_and_Leia_Organa.png|thumb|right|250px|Billie Lourd is the daughter of Carrie Fisher, the actress who portrayed Princess Leia Organa.]]
Kaydel Ko Connix was played by [[Billie Lourd]] in [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']] and [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']]. Lourd is the daughter of actress [[Carrie Fisher]], who played Leia Organa in the ''[[Star Wars]]'' saga. She originally auditioned for the main role of Rey, but lost out to [[Daisy Ridley]].<ref name="Billie As Rey">{{WebCite|url=http://ew.com/movies/2017/09/13/billie-lourd-rey-star-wars-carrie-fisher|text=Carrie Fisher's daughter, Billie Lourd, auditioned for ''Star Wars'' Rey role|author=Holub, Christian|date=2017-09-13|work=[[Wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|Entertainment Weekly]]|archivedate=20180805142032}}</ref> This in turn led ''The Force Awakens'' director [[J.J. Abrams]] to create Connix's character specifically for Lourd.<ref name="J.J. Father of Kaydel">{{WebCite|url=https://www.elitedaily.com/p/what-is-billie-lourds-role-in-the-last-jedi-kaydel-ko-connix-will-be-back-7218368|text=What Is Billie Lourd's Role In 'The Last Jedi'? Kaydel Ko Connix Will Be Back|author=Kickham, Dylan|date=2017-12-06|work=Elite Daily|archivedate=20180729081333}}</ref>

The character was listed as "Lieutenant Connix" in the end credits of ''The Force Awakens'', and was identified as "Kaydel Ko" in ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]'', a reference book written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] and released in conjunction with the film.<ref name="TFAVD" /> The name "Kaydel" comes from Kay Hidalgo,<ref name="Kaydel">{{Twitter|manraysky|status/1741986226167845287|Kay Hidalgo|date=2024-01-01|quote=[An image of Kaydel Ko Connix's Wookieepedia article] This is not a coincidence. 😂 {{C|In response to: Go to Wookieepedia, search for your first name, and see if any characters pop up! I actually got a few, along with a planet and system from the game TIE fighter.}}|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/80bEX}}</ref> a combination of her first name and the beginning of her maiden name, "Del."<ref name="Del Name">{{Twitter|manraysky|status/1741986382762193290|Kay Hidalgo|date=2024-01-01|quote="Del" is the beginning of my maiden name. {{C|In response to: [An image of Kaydel Ko Connix's Wookieepedia article] This is not a coincidence. 😂}}|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/Osbqo}}</ref>

